body:
@jycr could you try to add breakpoints and understand why the enhancement is not done?

The first step would probably be to check if entities are passed to the enhancer.

BTW, do you somehow have a special character in the path to your classes (space, non ascii characters)?

Hello @gsmet @FroMage ,

I think i have found the source of the problem. 
In the class [AugmentPhase](https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/blob/master/core/creator/src/main/java/io/quarkus/creator/phase/augment/AugmentPhase.java#L330) (line 330), you are doing this : 

```java
final String className = pathName.substring(0, pathName.length() - 6).replace('/', '.');
```

The problem on windows, is that the `pathName` contains `\` instead of `/`. So the replacement is doing nothing, and no visitor can be found due to this (the visitor has to be executed to enhance the panache entities classes).

```java
// The className should have all path separators replaced by '.' here
// In windows, as path separator is '\' and not '/', className has a bad value here
final List<BiFunction<String, ClassVisitor, ClassVisitor>> visitors = bytecodeTransformers.get(className);

// So here, visitors is empty because it can not be found in the bytecodeTransformers map
 if (visitors == null || visitors.isEmpty()) {
    return;
 }
```

A fix could be : 
```java
final String className = pathName.substring(0, pathName.length() - 6).replace(File.separatorChar, '.');
```

Hope it can help you to solve this problem.

Sylvain
